{
  "id": "number-theory",
  "title": "Number Theory from First Principles",
  "summary": "Proof-driven foundations from integer arithmetic, prime distribution and Dedekind ideals through quadratic forms and local fields. Includes complete proofs of Dirichlet’s theorem, the prime number theorem, finite p-adic extension structure, and rational Hilbert reciprocity.",
  "assumed_background": [
    "integer arithmetic, fractions, equations and basic algebra",
    "comfortable reading simple proofs helps; the Mathematical Reasoning and Proof course is optional preparation",
    "no group theory, field theory or analytic number theory assumed"
